\details{
The steps (Methods Section 7; SI Section 7):
\enumerate{
\item \strong{Forward.} The first signal is the unit's leader, the variant with
the smallest P value. In each round the selected variants are appended
to the covariates (they enter the mean of the intermediate values and
both boundary equations), the model without a test variant is refitted,
and every other variant of the cis window that \code{\link[=bohr_cis]{bohr_cis()}} tested is
tested again with the unit's own test: mu with the F-corrected
likelihood-ratio test, where the parameter count is the rank of the
conditional design on the intermediate samples plus one; p0 and p1 with
the Firth-penalised likelihood-ratio test. The conditional P values of
the window are combined with ACAT (\code{\link[=acat]{acat()}}, with the cap of the
\code{\link[=bohr_cis]{bohr_cis()}} call). The variant with the smallest conditional P value is
added as a new signal when this window P value is at most \code{threshold};
otherwise the unit stops. A unit stops at \code{max_signals} signals.
\item \strong{Backward.} For a unit with two or more signals, each signal is
retested conditional on the others: every variant of the window except
the other signals is tested, and the signal is kept when the ACAT P value
of this leave-one-out scan is at most \code{threshold}. A unit's only signal
is always kept. The leave-one-out scans are returned in \code{loo}; the
statistics of each signal's own variant in its scan (\verb{loo_*}) are the
per-signal conditional statistics used for colocalization.
}
The threshold of a tissue is its discovery threshold: the largest unit
P value with q at or below the false-discovery rate of the \code{\link[=bohr_cis]{bohr_cis()}}
call. Ties of the smallest P value go to the first variant in the order of
the rows of \code{genotype} (the VCF order in the paper).

\strong{Exact mirror pairs.} The units are those of \code{\link[=bohr_cis]{bohr_cis()}} after its
mirror rule: a boundary event of an exact mirror pair is a p0 unit at the
promoter that goes silent. With \code{absolute}, each significant p0 unit of a
\code{boundary_exact} pair is labelled by absolute activity (SI Section 2,
"Which promoter a boundary event regulates"): the absolute activity of each
promoter of the pair is regressed (least squares) on the leader's dosage,
with the covariates and the unit's other kept signals; a promoter changes
when \eqn{|z| \ge} \code{abs_z}. When only the other promoter changes, the
event is renamed p1 at that promoter (its P values are those of the p0
test, the same test); otherwise it stays p0 at the silent promoter. In the
paper no puQTL was renamed. Without \code{absolute}, the labels of \code{\link[=bohr_cis]{bohr_cis()}}
are kept (the paper's rule "v3m"), and \code{settings$mirror_labels} says so.

